<title>POLAND: POLL-POLISH 52-WK, 13-WK T-BILL YIELD SEEN DOWN.</title>
<headline>POLL-POLISH 52-WK, 13-WK T-BILL YIELD SEEN DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banks expect the average yield on Poland's benchmark 52-week T-bill to fall to 22.27 percent at the end of 1997 against 22.63 percent at Monday's primary sale, a Reuters poll of the country's 27 largest banks showed.</p>
<p>The average yield on the 13-week T-bill was also seen falling to 21.88 percent by year-end from 22.45 percent at today's primary auction, the poll showed.</p>
<p>But both predictions were higher than a month ago. @</p>
<p>		   AUGUST	  END-97	  12-MONTHS AHEAD</p>
<p> 52-WEEK AVG   22.65	22.27 (20.12)     20.10 (18.37)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   22.42	20.20 (14.90)     17.00 (13.20)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   23.60	23.50 (22.00)     23.50 (21.50)</p>
<p> 13-WEEK AVG   22.61	21.88 (19.61)     19.81 (17.88)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   22.19	19.79 (14.00)     16.50 (12.00)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   23.20	23.60 (22.00)     23.00 (21.00)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets previous figures for end-97 and July-98 from last month's poll.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
